# runtime data - regenerated by seed.py / created at runtime, never hand-authored
data/

# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# editor/OS cruft
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# MS Office temp/lock files (created while a doc is open, not real content)
~$*

# holds DATABASE_URL/SESSION_SECRET in plain text - never commit these.
# .env.production: generated by setup_production_services.ps1, read by run_service.bat.
# .env.development: generated once for the dev database, read by run_dev.bat.
.env.production
.env.development
# Plain `.env` too. The two names above were listed because they are the ones this repo's
# own scripts generate, which left a bare `.env` - the name every tutorial and library
# reaches for by default, and the name the Oracle deployment actually uses - tracked. A
# secret is compromised the moment it is committed, not when someone notices, so the
# catch-all matters more than the specific names.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# scheduled backups (see backup.ps1) - large, machine-specific, not source
/backups/

# Windows service stdout/stderr logs (see setup_production_services.ps1)
service_*.log
data/lumenpulse_cache/
data/exenia_cache/

# Large reference material, kept on disk but out of the repo. The 2026 and 2023 Exenia
# catalogues are 45MB and 33MB, and SampleInputOld another 16MB - 94MB against a 36MB repo,
# and Git history cannot be slimmed afterwards without rewriting it. Nothing reads them any
# more: every Exenia row now cites its own product page rather than a catalogue page (see
# import_exenia_website.py), so the products they described are already in the database with
# a better source. Keep your own copies; they are reference, not input.
SampleInputs/Exenia 2026 Catalogue.pdf
SampleInputs/Exenia 2023 Catalogue.pdf
SampleInputOld/

# Decorative-brand price lists and catalogues: about 760 MB of vendor PDFs, read in place by
# scripts/pricelists/. The same reasoning as above applies: one accidental `git add .` would put
# them in history for good. The two multiplier PNGs already tracked under DECORATIVE PRICE/
# stay tracked (.gitignore never untracks a file).
SampleInputs/DECORATIVE PRICE/
SampleInputs/Decorative Tab Inputs/

# Claude Code: settings.json is shared on purpose; these two are personal or runtime files.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# private interview notes
tut.md
